WEBVTT

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.340
Okay, are you ready to go?

00:00:06.340 --> 00:00:07.610
No.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:09.700
Don't be selfish.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.030
Mommy needs to go to work soon.

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.490
Please?

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.560
No! I don't wanna go!

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:21.200
Oh, Chisato-chan!

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:23.370
Eat it.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:24.180
Huh?

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:26.260
Eat it.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:50.720
Hey, wait!

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:51.460
Wait up!

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.840
Here, eat it.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:06.080
Here!

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:09.090
Hey...

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:10.250
Eat it!

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.480
How is it? Is it good?

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:16.900
Yeah.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.960
Eat it!

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:23.100
I don't want it.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:23.560
Huh?

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:26.000
I don't want it.

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:30.440
I don't want chocolate.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:34.240
<i>I don't want it.</i>

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.120
<i>I don't want chocolate.</i>

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.020
<i>I don't want to share a chocolate bar with you.</i>

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.460
Sorry! I'm so sorry!

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:54.740
I'll give you chocolate!

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:56.460
You can have some chocolate!

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:57.560
So please!

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.760
Don't disappear!

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:02.890
Don't disappear! Don't disappear!

00:02:02.890 --> 00:02:04.380
I'll give you chocolate!

00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.020
So promise me!

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:12.720
I won't disappear.

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:15.740
I'm not going anywhere.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:17.400
I promise.

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.990
I'll always stay by your side...

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:23.820
no matter what.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.920
Yuu-kun is okay, so don't cry.

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:08.390
You're still crying?

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:11.020
Yuu-kun! What did they say?

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:15.860
They said I'll be fine, but they want me to come back tomorrow for a reexamination, just in case.

00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:16.920
I see.

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:20.030
I'm so relieved that it wasn't anything serious.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:25.160
Huh? President Mouri?

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:27.280
Hey, Chisato?

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:38.250
Excuse me!

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.060
Oh, if it isn't Sacchan.

00:04:41.060 --> 00:04:44.200
Is it true that Oojima was involved in an accident?

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.890
He got hit by the store truck.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:55.190
He jumped out so suddenly that they couldn't stop in time.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.860
So how is he?!

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:00.280
He didn't really get hurt. He's doing just fine.

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:02.120
Yeah.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:05.800
Thank goodness.

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.940
He's such a troublemaker.

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:10.950
I feel sorry for the guy who hit him.

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:13.370
But it's great that no one got hurt.

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:17.120
He had me so worried. I was prepared for the worst!

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.880
He really needs to take care of himself. The election's in full swing, after all.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:26.180
I-I agree! He was so careless and made everyone worry.

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:27.960
Stupidjima!

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.700
S-Stupidjima?

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:32.850
I'm calling him Stupidjima because he's stupid! Is that a problem?

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:35.390
H-Hi.

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:40.060
Y-Yuu-kun. Are you all right?

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:44.820
Y-Yeah. At least... one of us is.

00:05:52.850 --> 00:05:54.830
You live next door.

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.500
I can't unlock the door like this.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.440
I kinda want to get changed.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:31.720
Isn't this Morishita-san's?

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:36.040
"Kana"?

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:40.700
What about food?

00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:47.340
I want to use the restroom.

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:50.260
I want to take a bath.

00:06:53.150 --> 00:06:55.680
Sorry, Chisato. I really am.

00:06:55.680 --> 00:06:56.880
It was my fault.

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:02.330
I didn't know that would happen.

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:03.900
I'll be more careful.

00:07:04.810 --> 00:07:07.000
It must've been a big shock for you,

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.360
but try to be more understanding.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:10.800
Please.

00:07:11.450 --> 00:07:13.120
Let go of me already.

00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:48.190
I know! I know what you're getting at!

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:50.610
But what am I supposed to do about it?

00:07:52.610 --> 00:07:53.700
Liar.

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:57.080
You said you wouldn't go anywhere.

00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:58.700
You promised me.

00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.420
I'm <i>not</i> going anywhere!

00:08:00.420 --> 00:08:01.220
Liar.

00:08:01.220 --> 00:08:02.420
I'm not lying!

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:03.560
Liar.

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:04.960
I'm right here!

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:05.790
I'm here for you right now!

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:08.320
Liar...

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:12.260
Liar, liar, liar, liar...

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:13.970
Liar!

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:39.660
Eat it.

00:08:41.150 --> 00:08:42.480
Eat it...

00:08:42.480 --> 00:08:43.660
Eat it!

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.020
Please eat it.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:50.860
Eat it and tell me it tastes good.

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:54.420
Eat it and forgive me.

00:08:55.270 --> 00:08:59.120
Don't leave me alone. Stay by my side.

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:00.630
Please.

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:02.000
Please!

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:05.520
Who... am I?

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.190
Who am I to you?

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:11.120
What?

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:15.380
Am I just a replacement for Daiki-kun?

00:09:16.250 --> 00:09:16.950
That's not it!

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:18.620
That's exactly it!

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:22.660
You don't see <i>me</i>.

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:26.460
You see Daiki-kun <i>through</i> me.

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:31.630
That's why this isn't love.

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:39.200
You mentioned how you felt so far away from me.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:41.660
I feel the same way.

00:09:42.210 --> 00:09:43.520
Yuuki...

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:46.020
I won't eat it anymore.

00:09:47.090 --> 00:09:49.800
You should eat it yourself, Chisato.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:52.980
I can't be a replacement for Daiki-kun anymore.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:55.640
Why? You said that you'd stay with me!

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:57.120
I <i>am</i> with you!

00:09:57.120 --> 00:10:00.200
Not as Daiki-kun, but as Oojima Yuuki!

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.410
So you should be the one to eat it, not me!

00:10:03.830 --> 00:10:05.200
You want to be with <i>me</i>, right?

00:10:05.610 --> 00:10:07.400
You want to see <i>me</i>, right?

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:13.590
I can be Oojima Yuuki, right?

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:46.600
I-I'm back, Morishita-san.

00:11:47.870 --> 00:11:49.040
Oojima.

00:11:49.040 --> 00:11:49.980
Welcome back.

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:52.000
Wh-Where is everyone?

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:53.980
Not here.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:55.060
I see.

00:11:55.060 --> 00:11:56.020
Oh, right.

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:57.730
Are the updated approval ratings out?

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:03.950
Things are looking pretty good for us!

00:12:10.010 --> 00:12:13.320
Oojima, not a happy color.

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:16.380
Because our President isn't coming?

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.000
That's half of the reason, I guess.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:20.970
Half?

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:22.840
Half of it is because of Chisato.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:24.040
The other half...

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:26.100
is pretty personal.

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:28.790
Oojima...

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:29.720
Oh, I almost forgot.

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:31.390
This is yours.

00:12:32.390 --> 00:12:36.980
Sorry. I took it with me by
mistake after the accident.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.400
I fixed it to make up for that.

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:42.030
Oojima, you knew how to fix it?

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:44.400
I looked up how to online.

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:46.030
It wasn't too hard.

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:09.480
What was that song?

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:11.440
I don't know.

00:13:11.440 --> 00:13:12.080
Huh?

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:14.730
I only learned how to play it.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:17.150
Did a person named Kana teach you?

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:19.650
The name carved on the back.

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:23.680
This is Kana's.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:25.400
She gave it to me.

00:13:25.400 --> 00:13:27.940
I see. You must've been good friends.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:30.460
Kana is my best friend,

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:34.140
but I suddenly lost contact with her.

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:36.290
She went missing?

00:13:36.650 --> 00:13:41.300
I came to Takafuji to find Kana...

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:42.960
But...

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:46.260
So she's a student here.

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:50.080
Where are you, Kana?

00:14:09.930 --> 00:14:10.910
Kana!

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:14.720
President, what's the matter?

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:17.290
Oh, please excuse me.

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:20.040
I nearly lost my balance and tripped at the entrance.

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:22.460
O-Okay...

00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:26.440
By the way, what happened to your campaign manager?

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:28.340
I couldn't get in touch with her.

00:14:28.340 --> 00:14:30.760
Um, well...

00:14:30.760 --> 00:14:33.960
She wasn't feeling well, so she's taking the day off.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:35.520
I see.

00:14:35.520 --> 00:14:39.900
She asked me for advice yesterday, and there's more I'd like to discuss.

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:41.690
Advice? On what?

00:14:44.390 --> 00:14:45.480
Oojima-kun,

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:51.120
is it true that you want to address the discrimination against financial aid students in your manifesto?

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:53.640
Huh? Y-Yes.

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:57.880
I'm still formulating the policy, though. I'm not sure what to do.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:15:00.040
Please discard that policy.

00:15:01.370 --> 00:15:04.960
Please don't touch on matters concerning financial aid students in this election.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.840
But there are students suffering—

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:10.760
This is not a request. It's an order.

00:15:11.110 --> 00:15:12.720
Are we clear, Oojima-kun?

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:17.100
We're cooperating with you to get you elected.

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:23.140
We're not supporting you so that you can push for acceptance of your personal opinions.

00:15:23.140 --> 00:15:24.270
That's so...

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:28.000
It's possible to resolve the issue <i>after</i> you get elected,

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:30.530
but you won't be able to do anything if you lose the race.

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:35.560
Admirable calls for change will achieve nothing unless you have the means.

00:15:36.910 --> 00:15:41.670
Do you understand how to go about making your ideal a reality?

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:51.100
The President's <i>still</i> supporting that guy?

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:54.930
He's wasting his time. All the arrangements have already been made.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:57.720
Okay, don't worry about a thing.

00:15:57.720 --> 00:16:00.780
I'll protect the Takafuji tradition.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:03.260
Rest assured, Katahira-senpai.

00:16:04.070 --> 00:16:06.690
Oh, yeah. On a related note...

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:07.230
Hatsushiba General Hospital Emergency Entrance

00:16:07.230 --> 00:16:09.190
I have a request.

00:16:10.350 --> 00:16:14.340
Ooshima-san, please come to the accounting desk.

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:15.640
It's Oojima!

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:18.820
S-Sorry!

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:20.370
Huh? Haida-san?

00:16:21.430 --> 00:16:23.460
O-Oojima-kun!

00:16:25.370 --> 00:16:27.640
I'm so sorry! Did it hurt?

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:31.340
No, I'm just having trouble with my contacts,

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.100
so I'm here to see an ophthalmologist.

00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:34.640
I see.

00:16:34.640 --> 00:16:36.220
How about you, Oojima-kun?

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:38.390
I was in a small car accident.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:46.380
Hey, it's not that big of a deal.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:49.260
That's not it. I just dropped my contact.

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:49.880
Huh?

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:51.530
Where?

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:53.400
It probably fell around here.

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:56.190
Where is it?

00:16:56.190 --> 00:16:56.910
Where...

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:00.380
Excuse me, Haida-san.

00:17:00.380 --> 00:17:01.600
I'll see you later!

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:15.530
What's the meaning of this?!

00:17:15.530 --> 00:17:17.300
This isn't what we agreed on!

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:19.470
I accepted your conditions!

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:22.180
<i>Who is he talking to?</i>

00:17:22.510 --> 00:17:24.400
I am a member of the Public Safety Commission.

00:17:24.400 --> 00:17:25.920
I understand that.

00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:29.180
However, this is an entirely different matter!

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:30.440
This was a legitimate deal!

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:32.690
<i>A deal?</i>

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:36.440
It's entirely Oosawa-kun's fault that we had to withdraw from the election!

00:17:36.440 --> 00:17:37.360
It has nothing to do with me!

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:39.980
<i>Oosawa...</i>

00:17:39.980 --> 00:17:41.400
<i>From the Oosawa Incident?</i>

00:17:41.400 --> 00:17:43.380
That was the condition!

00:17:43.380 --> 00:17:46.470
Please don't abandon Kana!

00:17:46.470 --> 00:17:47.370
<i>Kana...</i>

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:54.840
I understand. Give me some time to think.

00:17:56.190 --> 00:17:57.000
Good-bye.

00:18:38.530 --> 00:18:40.100
A dead end?

00:18:44.730 --> 00:18:47.600
Oogibashi... Kana?

00:19:04.730 --> 00:19:06.080
Sorry!

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:19.440
Is this the Kana that they were talking about?

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:21.220
What business do you have with her?

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:23.300
P-President...

00:19:36.190 --> 00:19:37.100
What's this?

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:39.320
Enough.

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:41.180
There's no point in subjecting him to this.

00:19:43.050 --> 00:19:45.600
Promise me you won't put up a struggle.

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:47.330
If you do, we'll remove your handcuffs.

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:48.920
Sound good?

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:51.220
Yeah.

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:56.630
So how much have you figured out?

00:19:56.630 --> 00:19:57.700
Huh?

00:19:57.700 --> 00:19:59.440
Answer me honestly.

00:19:59.950 --> 00:20:05.240
I don't want to resort to violence, and if possible, I'd like to remain on good terms with you.

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:09.060
I am a former Public Safety Commissioner.

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:13.810
I can't hold a candle to Oosawa-kun, but I'm capable of being merciless, myself.

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:18.940
You're asking about how much I know about Kana-san, right?

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:20.360
Indeed.

00:20:21.310 --> 00:20:23.200
Oogibashi Kana.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:26.120
She owns the harmonica that Morishita-san carries around.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:29.060
You made a deal to recover her consciousness.

00:20:29.060 --> 00:20:30.520
Oosawa's involved.

00:20:31.070 --> 00:20:32.840
I've made a grave blunder.

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:36.750
I was certainly very startled at the time, but I can't believe I failed to notice that I was being overheard.

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:38.940
What is this about?

00:20:38.940 --> 00:20:40.760
What are you people doing?

00:20:41.450 --> 00:20:44.260
If you really want to know, I'll tell you everything.

00:20:44.260 --> 00:20:47.300
However, there's no going back once you hear it.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:51.240
F-Fine by me.

00:20:51.240 --> 00:20:52.230
All right.

00:20:53.230 --> 00:20:57.920
We, the Public Safety Commission, maintain security on campus,

00:20:57.920 --> 00:21:03.280
but we can't possibly keep every part of this large school under control.

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:06.180
So we use less than admirable methods.

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:07.660
Less than admirable?

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:09.540
They're called S-agents.

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:12.460
Put simply, they're spies.

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:13.290
Spies?!

00:21:13.650 --> 00:21:20.520
Attending the school as normal students, they secretly keep an eye on other students

00:21:20.520 --> 00:21:23.300
and provide the Public Safety Commission with intelligence.

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:29.300
This system allows the Commission to deal with issues before they develop into serious incidents.

00:21:30.030 --> 00:21:36.000
Once an S-agent completes their orientation and training, they are assigned to an officer.

00:21:36.000 --> 00:21:39.940
Oogibashi Kana was one of the agents assigned to me.

00:21:40.630 --> 00:21:42.320
The other one was...

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:43.780
Morishita Michiru.

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:55.380
Would you like me to continue?

00:21:56.390 --> 00:21:59.290
I've already told you far too much for you to go back.

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:24.570
In the classroom, looking out the window,
kyoushitsu no madobe de nagameru

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:28.530
Watching the sky fade softly into twilight,
yasashii yuugure no sora

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:32.670
I turn around, and there you are again
furimukeba kimi ga egao de

00:22:32.670 --> 00:22:36.750
Looking at me, you smile
kocchi wo miteta

00:22:36.750 --> 00:22:41.090
"Let's go home," you always say,
issho ni kaerou itsumo no

00:22:41.090 --> 00:22:45.250
Going all the places we go every day
toomawari wo shinagara

00:22:45.260 --> 00:22:49.280
Your fingers are just a step away
mada sukoshi todokanai

00:22:49.280 --> 00:22:55.760
But deep inside me, it hurts not holding your hand
yubisaki ga tada setsunakute

00:22:57.390 --> 00:23:02.400
In my heart, I found all these hopes and dreams
ano hi kimi to meguriaeta kara

00:23:02.400 --> 00:23:06.570
Because on that day we happened to meet
takusan no yume wo mitsuketan da

00:23:06.570 --> 00:23:08.760
Even when I wanted to cry,
nakitai toki demo

00:23:08.760 --> 00:23:12.460
You always stayed right there by my side
itsumo soba ni ite kurete

00:23:12.460 --> 00:23:14.990
I want to thank you so much
doumo arigatou

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:19.250
What I wrote on that page I hid from you
no-to ni kaita himitsu no pe-ji wa

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:23.130
Were the words that I just couldn't say
zutto iezu ni ita kotoba

00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:28.890
Now they float forever as whispers on the wind
ima kaze no naka zutto sasayaku yo nee

00:23:28.890 --> 00:23:36.760
Listen close, it says, "I love you so much"
kiite kimi ga daisuki da yo

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:44.880
We're conducting a survey.

00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:47.340
What kind of snacks do you like?

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:49.160
Tasty snacks.

00:23:50.090 --> 00:23:52.260
What about the kind of snacks you dislike?

00:23:52.800 --> 00:23:54.360
Untasty snacks.

00:23:55.010 --> 00:23:57.040
All right, let's try a different question.

00:23:57.040 --> 00:24:00.170
Which do you prefer, Western sweets or Japanese sweets?

00:24:00.170 --> 00:24:01.180
Normal.

00:24:01.180 --> 00:24:03.800
No, that doesn't answer the question!

00:24:03.800 --> 00:24:07.960
Next time, Episode 11: "Investigation!"

00:24:07.960 --> 00:24:10.580
So you're fine with anything edible. Got it.
